dialect protocol
protocol stdio.gif.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.gif
start header

# Real GIF87a §18-27 file structure, matching this artifact's real `encode_gif`/`decode_gif`
# (../../⚙️engine/🦀️.rs) field-for-field: 6-byte ASCII magic "GIF87a", then the
# Logical Screen Descriptor (width/height u16LE x2, one packed flags byte incl. GCT-present/
# color-resolution/sort/GCT-size, bg color index, pixel aspect ratio) — ALL real, individually
# walked fields, exactly matching PNG's own IHDR treatment (P2-M2's own worked PNG example).
#
# This is the SEMIO-envelope-UNWRAPPED payload (P2-M3 §3/§5 point 4) — `GifSnapshot::
# encode_pack_with` (../../🦀️.rs) is `encode_gif(self)` wrapped by `store::
# semio_format::wrap_binary`, so the bytes this file walks start exactly where the envelope's
# own 8-byte magic + u32le token-length + token hand off (described once, framework-side, at
# 🧰️framework/…/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️.protocol.semio) — NOT re-described here.
#
# P2-FG2 NEW mechanism-gap, confirmed live (not assumed) by a real `walk_protocol` run:
# `framing magic` unconditionally reads EXACTLY 8 bytes for its byte-check, regardless of how
# many hex digits the declared literal has (`0x474946383761`, GIF87a's real 6-byte "GIF87a"
# signature, still got read/compared as `[0,0,71,73,70,56,55,97]` — an 8-byte, left-zero-
# padded value — against the real on-disk 6-byte magic immediately followed by 2 real screen-
# descriptor bytes, a genuine mismatch). Every existing real `framing magic` precedent in this
# repo (PNG's 8-byte signature, the framework's own SEMIO-envelope magic, the `.spk` container
# magic) happens to be exactly 8 bytes — this is the first artifact whose real magic is
# SHORTER. Recorded as `protocol-framing-magic-fixed-8-bytes` (not yet in the recipe's §5
# table). Modeled honestly: `framing record` (no magic byte-check) + a real, individually-read
# `field magic fixed 6` — genuinely walked but not byte-validated at the PROTOCOL layer
# (the real Rust `decode_gif` already validates it byte-for-byte, `data[0..6] != b"GIF87a"`).
framing record

header fixed 13
field magic fixed 6
field width u16
field height u16
field packed u8
field bg_color_index u8
field pixel_aspect_ratio u8

# Past the fixed 13-byte magic + Logical Screen Descriptor, the real remaining bytes are: an OPTIONAL
# Global Color Table (`3 * 2^((packed & 0x07) + 1)` bytes, present iff `packed & 0x80 != 0`),
# then a repeated block sequence (0x2C Image Descriptor + optional Local Color Table + a
# LZW-compressed sub-block chain, terminated by the 0x3B trailer byte) — a genuine, real
# tag-dispatched `repeat` shape (§2.3), same construct PNG's own chunk loop uses.
#
# This artifact CANNOT express that `repeat` here, for TWO independent, genuine dialect
# reasons (neither is a PNG-style single-arm gap — both block the ENTIRE remainder, not one
# arm):
#   (a) `packed`'s GCT-presence bit IS testable (`Cond`'s `ge`/`eq` against the whole `packed`
#       byte value can gate presence), but the GCT's own BYTE LENGTH is `3 * 2^(size+1)` where
#       `size` is `packed`'s low 3 BITS — this dialect has no bitfield/sub-byte field
#       decomposition primitive at all (confirmed by reading `Prim`/`Cond`'s full grammar,
#       §2.2/§2.3 of the recipe) and no arithmetic-expression `Array` count source (`Count`
#       binds only to a literal `Fixed(n)`, `Varint`, or a named `Field`, never `field * k`).
#   (b) Since the GCT's own length can never be computed, the repeated block sequence's own
#       START position is unknowable declaratively — `repeat`'s own tag-dispatch (§2.3) needs
#       a known starting offset, which nothing past `packed` can supply.
# Recorded as a NEW mechanism-gap (not yet in the recipe's §5 consolidated table):
# `protocol-bitfield-bytelen-computation` — packed-byte bit-subfields driving a computed
# Array/segment byte length. The Rust `encode_gif`/`decode_gif` side IS genuinely, fully
# structured (real bit-shift GCT-size decode, real tag-dispatched block loop, real LZW
# sub-block chain) — this is purely a limit on how deep the PROTOCOL DESCRIPTION can validate
# structurally past the fixed screen descriptor, same documented-limitation shape as PNG's own
# `protocol-repeat-length-not-named`/DWG's encrypted-segment carve-out (§6).
chain rest bytes
